1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,615
Visitors expect to find a page by typing a few words.

2
00:00:04,615 --> 00:00:08,965
In this video, let's set up site search for an Orchard Core site:

3
00:00:08,965 --> 00:00:14,051
the features, an index, the default index, the permission for visitors, and a

4
00:00:14,051 --> 00:00:15,950
search box on your pages.

5
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:23,832
An index stores your content items for searching.

6
00:00:23,832 --> 00:00:28,129
By default, a search looks words up in the full text of each item:

7
00:00:28,129 --> 00:00:29,859
its title and its body.

8
00:00:29,859 --> 00:00:35,170
When someone publishes, changes or removes an item, Orchard Core updates the index.

9
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:39,117
A search provider creates and queries indexes.

10
00:00:39,117 --> 00:00:44,098
Elasticsearch and Azure AI Search keep their indexes in a separate service.

11
00:00:44,098 --> 00:00:48,648
Lucene keeps its indexes in files on the server that runs your site,

12
00:00:48,648 --> 00:00:50,370
so this video uses it.

13
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:55,010
The Search feature adds the search page and the Search Form widget.

14
00:00:55,010 --> 00:00:59,060
Visitors need permission to query an index, which you grant to a role.

15
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:06,646
Let's start at Search, Indexes, on a Blog site.

16
00:01:06,646 --> 00:01:08,073
Select Add index:

17
00:01:08,073 --> 00:01:13,157
the dialog lists the available sources, and with no provider enabled it asks

18
00:01:13,157 --> 00:01:16,940
you to enable a feature which provides an index source.

19
00:01:17,526 --> 00:01:20,891
Open Tools, Features, and filter the list for Lucene.

20
00:01:20,891 --> 00:01:24,996
Select Enable on the row named Lucene, and the page reloads with a

21
00:01:24,996 --> 00:01:27,106
message that names the feature.

22
00:01:27,573 --> 00:01:30,090
Search is the second feature to enable.

23
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:35,011
Filter the list for frontend search, words from its description, and select Enable

24
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,353
on the Search row.

25
00:01:40,578 --> 00:01:43,649
Back at Search, Indexes, select Add index.

26
00:01:43,649 --> 00:01:47,871
The Available Sources dialog groups the sources by provider.

27
00:01:47,871 --> 00:01:52,925
Under Lucene, Content in Lucene builds an index from the content items of

28
00:01:52,925 --> 00:01:54,908
your site, so select Add.

29
00:01:55,417 --> 00:01:59,265
Index Name is the name of the index in the provider, and it

30
00:01:59,265 --> 00:02:01,751
cannot change once the index exists.

31
00:02:01,751 --> 00:02:07,138
Name is the unique name that the settings, the permission and the search address use.

32
00:02:07,138 --> 00:02:10,157
Type website in Index Name, and Name follows.

33
00:02:10,612 --> 00:02:15,112
Content types lists the types to index, and at least one is required.

34
00:02:15,112 --> 00:02:17,212
Select Blog Post and Article.

35
00:02:17,212 --> 00:02:21,892
Culture stays on Any culture, and the other options keep their defaults.

36
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:23,357
Select Save.

37
00:02:23,357 --> 00:02:28,839
A message confirms that the index was created and that synchronizing runs in the background.

38
00:02:28,839 --> 00:02:32,810
The index appears in the list with the labels Lucene and Content.

39
00:02:37,063 --> 00:02:39,635
Open Settings, Search, Site Search.

40
00:02:39,635 --> 00:02:43,212
Default search index lists the indexes you created.

41
00:02:43,212 --> 00:02:48,923
Select website, which the search page queries unless the address names another index.

42
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:53,513
Placeholder is the text that the search box of the search page shows

43
00:02:53,513 --> 00:02:55,117
before a visitor types.

44
00:02:55,117 --> 00:02:58,159
Enter Search articles and posts, and select Save.

45
00:03:02,399 --> 00:03:07,502
A visitor can only search an index that the visitor has permission to query.

46
00:03:07,502 --> 00:03:13,539
Open Access Control, Roles, and edit Anonymous, the role of visitors who are not signed in.

47
00:03:14,047 --> 00:03:18,620
Filter the permissions for Query 'website' Index, and select it.

48
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:20,123
Then select Save.

49
00:03:20,123 --> 00:03:26,787
The permission Query any index covers every index, and the Administrator role has it by default.

50
00:03:31,087 --> 00:03:33,819
A widget puts the search box on your pages.

51
00:03:33,819 --> 00:03:38,836
Open Design, Widgets, where zones are the regions of a page in which widgets appear.

52
00:03:38,836 --> 00:03:42,627
In the Footer zone, select Add Widget, and choose Search Form.

53
00:03:43,141 --> 00:03:48,594
Enter a Title, and select the Always layer, so the widget appears on every page.

54
00:03:48,594 --> 00:03:52,779
Enter a Placeholder for the widget's box, which is required.

55
00:03:52,779 --> 00:03:57,471
Leave Index Name empty to use the default index, and select Publish.

56
00:04:01,716 --> 00:04:03,404
Let's search as a visitor:

57
00:04:03,404 --> 00:04:05,304
this browser is not signed in.

58
00:04:05,304 --> 00:04:08,734
The search box sits at the bottom of the home page, so type

59
00:04:08,734 --> 00:04:10,476
harvest, and select Search.

60
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:14,419
The search page lists the content items that match:

61
00:04:14,419 --> 00:04:16,518
the two posts that mention harvest.

62
00:04:16,518 --> 00:04:18,771
Each result links to its content item.

63
00:04:19,237 --> 00:04:21,494
Let's clear the search box of the page:

64
00:04:21,494 --> 00:04:25,457
once it is empty, it shows the placeholder from the Site Search settings.

65
00:04:25,927 --> 00:04:28,416
A search that matches nothing says so.

66
00:04:28,416 --> 00:04:30,056
Let's search for zebra:

67
00:04:30,056 --> 00:04:33,507
the page shows the message "There are no such results."

68
00:04:37,707 --> 00:04:40,706
An index follows your content on its own.

69
00:04:40,706 --> 00:04:44,536
When an index falls out of step, open Search, Indexes:

70
00:04:44,536 --> 00:04:50,152
each index offers Synchronize, Reset and Rebuild, and a separate video covers when

71
00:04:50,152 --> 00:04:51,557
to use each one.

72
00:04:53,557 --> 00:04:57,950
A search provider, an index, the Search feature and a query permission give

73
00:04:57,950 --> 00:05:02,776
visitors a search page, and the Search Form widget adds a search box to your pages.

74
00:05:02,776 --> 00:05:04,187
Thanks for watching.

